<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Goldbeter, Gonze & Pourquié (2007) / Baker, Schnell & Maini (2006) RA–FGF8/Wnt mutual cross-inhibition bistable determination wavefront in vertebrate somitogenesis — MorphoEval overall 59.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 baseline assessment of `2012-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront.py` (59.6/100). The initial baseline implements the Goldbeter, Gonze & Pourquié (2007) CYP26A1 Hill induction C(F) and inverse hysteresis S-curve M(F) with saddle-node thresholds [M_1, M_2] = [1.0254, 3.3038] nM, but requires full 1D coupled RA-FGF8/Wnt reaction-diffusion PDE integration quantifying the 10-90% determination front jump width Delta_x_front << lambda_M, explicit opposing Vitamin A Deficiency (VAD) vs exogenous RA and SU5402 perturbation simulations with a CYP26-null monostable negative control, and bilateral dorsal somite segmentation against the vendored avian/vertebrate SEM specimen (`chick_ra_fgf_somites_specimen.jpg`). Overall 59.5/100 (faithfulness 57.6, reproducibility 63.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 63, Morphological realism / specimen match 54, Parameter expressivity 60, Morphometric validation 55, Source and data traceability 66, Code-to-model traceability 62, Reproducibility package 63. Output judged: docs/media/fgf_wnt_bistable_wavefront_comparison.png: rendered output of 2012-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 1336827 B, 2352×1372 px, artifact_sha256 499ddc7eed5384bbf4d6f0118814a3c67b19b1d52d6608fcfe526a0864146bde (sha256 499ddc7eed5384bbf4d6f0118814a3c67b19b1d52d6608fcfe526a0864146bde), spec_fingerprint 067326af3885ea73d93878ed07f29a5a29f47fffe07fbd95bba8a7110f414601. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 067326af3885ea73d93878ed07f29a5a29f47fffe07fbd95bba8a7110f414601; artifact_sha256: 499ddc7eed5384bbf4d6f0118814a3c67b19b1d52d6608fcfe526a0864146bde; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/fgf_wnt_bistable_wavefront/chick_ra_fgf_somites_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2..., datasets/fgf_wnt_bistable_wavefront/fgf_wnt_bistable_wavefront_reference.json=42c6196ddd32cee9..., datasets/fgf_wnt_bistable_wavefront/scout_manifest.json=783faa9ee6b3db0c...}." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Segment both bilateral dorsal paraxial somite rows on `datasets/fgf_wnt_bistable_wavefront/chick_ra_fgf_somites_specimen.jpg` and compute phase-aligned Pearson r correlation against the bistable wavefront-gated somite train.",
        "remediation needed: Simulate all 5 RA/FGF8 perturbation regimes (Wild-Type, Vitamin A Deficiency VAD v_sc=0.08 nM/min, Exogenous RA v_sc=0.42 nM/min, SU5402 FGFR1 inhibition, and Ectopic FGF8 bead) plus CYP26-null monostable (k_d1=0, n=0) and constitutive-FGF negative controls.",
        "remediation needed: Solve the 1D coupled RA-FGF8/Wnt reaction-diffusion PDE system along the 1000 um chick PSM and verify that the 10-90% bistable switch width Delta_x_front (~16.2 um) is >14-fold sharper than the exponential fgf8 mRNA decay length lambda_M = 360.67 um." ;
    pk:hasScore 5.95e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Goldbeter, Gonze & Pourquié (2007) / Baker, Schnell & Maini (2006) RA–FGF8/Wnt mutual cross-inhibition bistable determination wavefront in vertebrate somitogenesis — Parameter expressivity: 60/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
